Next link: [guides/native_shell.md](../../../../guides/native_shell.md)

Use `--local` when you need maintainer/local-dev proof.

This workspace is `host-owned` and `editable` after generation. Crosswake created
the scaffold so you can review and extend it, but it does not retain ownership of
the native project files.

## Phase 1 Boundary

- This is a Phase 1 route-policy handoff, not a proven shell runtime.
- Shell boot, manifest activation, bridge execution, and WebView behavior land in
  later phases.
- Keep the generated fixture local so the host team can evolve the native shell
  without confusing it for library-owned runtime code.

## Included Files

- `app/src/main/java/dev/crosswake/shell/AppShell.kt` - narrow placeholder source
- `app/src/main/assets/phase1_route_policy.json` - local bundled fixture for handoff work

## Next Step

Run `mix crosswake.install` first so the Phoenix host has a router-local policy
surface before you wire any native shell behavior.
